, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.5, "y": 21.6, "width": 70.1, "height": 3.4, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.5, "y": 21.6, "width": 70.1, "height": 3.4, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.5, "y": 21.6, "width": 70.1, "height": 3.4, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Define x_ijk to be the amount that agent j wants to assign in consumption for household i of commodity k."]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.5, "y": 27.2, "width": 36.5, "height": 3.9, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.5, "y": 27.2, "width": 36.5, "height": 3.9, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.5, "y": 27.2, "width": 36.5, "height": 3.9, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Arrow (1969) illustrates the general point:"]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 31.1, "width": 70.8, "height": 20.8, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 31.1, "width": 70.8, "height": 20.8, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 31.1, "width": 70.8, "height": 20.8, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Consider a pure exchange economy. Let xik be the amount of the k-th commodity consumed by the i-th individual (i = 1, ..., n; k = 1, ..., m) and xjk be the amount of the k-th commodity available. Suppose in general that the utility of the i-th individual is a function of the consumption of all individuals (not all types of consumption for all individuals need actually enter into any given individual's utility function); the utility of the i-th individual can be written Ui(x11, ..., xinm). We have the obvious constraints."]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 39.800000000000026, "y": 54.7, "width": 45.642114962727945, "height": 13.899999999999988, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 39.800000000000026, "y": 54.7, "width": 45.642114962727945, "height": 13.899999999999988, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["equation"]}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 39.800000000000026, "y": 54.7, "width": 45.642114962727945, "height": 13.899999999999988, "rotation": 0, "text": ["\u2211 xik \u2264 xk (17)\nxjik = xik, j = 1, ..., n (18)\n"]}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 70.8, "width": 71, "height": 24.7, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_7", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 70.8, "width": 71, "height": 24.7, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_7", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 70.8, "width": 71, "height": 24.7, "rotation": 0, "text": ["With this notation a Pareto-efficient allocation is a vector maximum of the utility functions Ui(xj11, ..., xjnm), subject to the constraints (17) and (18). Because of the notation used, the variables appearing in the utility function relating to the j-th individual are proper to him alone and appear in no one else's utility function. If we understand now that there are n^2m commodities (n values for i and for j, m values for k), indexed by the triple subscript jik, then the Pareto-efficiency problem has a thoroughly classical form. There are n^2m prices, Pjik, attached to the constraints (18), plus m prices qk, corresponding to constraints (17)."]}, "id": "BB_7", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 24.424342105263158, "y": 0.8223684210526315, "width": 24.88692434210526, "height": 1.8092105263157894, "rotation": 0}, "id": "_-TTvnaSMK", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 24.424342105263158, "y": 0.8223684210526315, "width": 24.88692434210526, "height": 1.8092105263157894, "rotati